# Line endings, settled 2026-09-16. Before this there was no policy: core.autocrlf
# was false, 31 scripts held CRLF and 23 held LF, and a tool that rewrote a file
# with \n turned a three-line edit into a 630-line diff. Two automatic commits on
# 2026-09-16 contain exactly that noise, which buries the real change.
#
# Git stores LF. Text is normalised on the way in, whatever the editor did.
* text=auto eol=lf

# PowerShell keeps CRLF in the working tree: the tooling, signing and ISE all
# expect it, and a .ps1 is the one file type here that is executed by Windows
# itself rather than by python.
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf

# Data the project reads and writes. Declared text so diffs stay readable and
# so a csv written by python does not churn against one written by PowerShell.
*.csv  text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.md   text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
*.yml  text eol=lf

# Never touched: binary, and a mangled byte here is a lost photograph.
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.png  binary
*.gif  binary
*.mp4  binary
*.mov  binary
*.db   binary
*.npy  binary
*.pickle binary
